# 03 — Multi-Viewport Layout (ViewportGrid)

## 1. Concept

Like 3ds Max, Blender, and SolidWorks — the viewport area can be split into multiple panes showing the same model from different perspectives and with different display modes.

## 2. Layout Presets

```typescript
export type ViewportGridLayout =
  | "single"        // 1×1 — full viewport
  | "split-h"       // 1×2 — left + right
  | "split-v"       // 2×1 — top + bottom
  | "quad"           // 2×2 — four equal panes
  | "one-plus-two"   // large left + two stacked right
  | "one-plus-three"; // large top + three below
```

### Visual

```
single:        split-h:       split-v:       quad:
┌──────────┐   ┌─────┬─────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌─────┬─────┐
│          │   │     │     │  │          │  │     │     │
│  persp.  │   │  L  │  R  │  │   top    │  │ TL  │ TR  │
│          │   │     │     │  ├──────────┤  ├─────┼─────┤
└──────────┘   └─────┴─────┘  │  bottom  │  │ BL  │ BR  │
                               └──────────┘  └─────┴─────┘

one-plus-two:          one-plus-three:
┌────────┬────┐        ┌──────────────┐
│        │ R1 │        │    main      │
│  main  ├────┤        ├────┬────┬────┤
│        │ R2 │        │ B1 │ B2 │ B3 │
└────────┴────┘        └────┴────┴────┘
```

## 3. Pane Configuration

Each pane has independent configuration:

```typescript
export interface ViewportPaneConfig {
  id: string;                          // "tl" | "tr" | "bl" | "br" | "main" | "left" | "right" | ...
  cameraPreset: CameraPreset;         // initial camera
  displayMode: DisplayMode;           // shaded, wireframe, etc.
  projection: ProjectionType;         // perspective | orthographic
  label: string;                      // "Perspective" | "Top" | "Front" | "Right"
  cameraLinked: boolean;              // if true, follows master pane camera
}

export type CameraPreset =
  | "perspective"
  | "top"
  | "bottom"
  | "front"
  | "back"
  | "left"
  | "right"
  | "isometric";

export type ProjectionType = "perspective" | "orthographic";
```

### Default Presets by Layout

| Layout | Panes |
|---|---|
| `single` | `[{ perspective, shaded }]` |
| `split-h` | `[{ perspective, shaded }, { top, wireframe, ortho }]` |
| `split-v` | `[{ perspective, shaded }, { front, wireframe, ortho }]` |
| `quad` | `[{ perspective, shaded }, { top, wireframe, ortho }, { front, wireframe, ortho }, { right, wireframe, ortho }]` |
| `one-plus-two` | `[{ perspective, shaded }, { top, wireframe, ortho }, { front, wireframe, ortho }]` |

## 4. Architecture

### Component Tree

```
ViewportGrid
  ├── ViewportPane (id="tl")
  │     ├── <canvas>
  │     ├── SceneController (owns Three.js)
  │     ├── DirtyRenderLoop
  │     └── PaneLabel overlay
  ├── ViewportPane (id="tr")
  │     └── ...
  ├── ViewportPane (id="bl")
  │     └── ...
  └── ViewportPane (id="br")
        └── ...
```

### ViewportGrid Component

```typescript
export function ViewportGrid({
  renderModel,
  kernel,
}: {
  renderModel: Viewport3DRenderModel | null;
  kernel: KernelApi;
}) {
  const layout = useViewport3DStore((s) => s.gridLayout);
  const panes = useViewport3DStore((s) => s.panes);
  const activePaneId = useViewport3DStore((s) => s.activePaneId);

  return (
    <div
      className="fm-viewport-grid"
      data-layout={layout}
    >
      {panes.map((pane) => (
        <ViewportPane
          key={pane.id}
          config={pane}
          renderModel={renderModel}
          isActive={pane.id === activePaneId}
          onActivate={() => setActivePane(pane.id)}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### CSS Grid Layouts

```css
.fm-viewport-grid {
  display: grid;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  gap: 2px;
  background: var(--fm-viewport-grid-gap-color);
}

.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="single"] {
  grid-template: 1fr / 1fr;
}

.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="split-h"] {
  grid-template: 1fr / 1fr 1fr;
}

.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="split-v"] {
  grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 1fr;
}

.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="quad"] {
  grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 1fr 1fr;
}

.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="one-plus-two"] {
  grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 2fr 1fr;
}
.fm-viewport-grid[data-layout="one-plus-two"] > :first-child {
  grid-row: 1 / -1;
}
```

## 5. Per-Pane Resource Sharing

All panes share the **same** `Viewport3DRenderModel` (same topology, field data, selection). The differences are:

| Shared across panes | Per-pane |
|---|---|
| Topology geometry data | Camera position/orientation |
| Field buffer data | Display mode |
| Selection identity | Projection type |
| Layer visibility (from command) | Label |
| Clipping config | Active/focused state |

**GPU resource sharing:** Each pane has its own `SceneController` and `WebGLRenderer`. Three.js `BufferGeometry` can be shared between scenes when panes use the same topology. The `MeshLayerRenderer` should check topology revision and reuse the geometry object if unchanged.

## 6. Camera Linking

Two modes:

### Independent (default)
Each pane has its own camera. Mouse interaction in one pane affects only that pane.

### Linked
One pane is designated master. Other linked panes derive their camera from the master but maintain their preset orientation offset.

```typescript
export function deriveLinkedCamera(
  master: CameraState,
  preset: CameraPreset,
): CameraState {
  // Linked panes follow master's target and distance
  // but apply their own orientation from the preset
  return {
    target: master.target,
    distance: master.distance,
    up: presetUp(preset),
    azimuth: presetAzimuth(preset),
    elevation: presetElevation(preset),
  };
}
```

Camera linking is toggled per-pane via the toolbar or `Ctrl+L` shortcut.

## 7. Active Pane

One pane is "active" at a time (blue border). The active pane:
- Receives keyboard shortcuts
- Is the target for toolbar commands
- Is shown maximized on double-click of pane label
- Camera controls apply to active pane

Clicking inside a pane makes it active.

## 8. Pane Maximise

Double-clicking the pane label temporarily maximises that pane to fill the entire viewport area. Double-click again to restore the grid layout. This is purely CSS — no unmounting of other panes (their render loops just stop because they're zero-size and the resize observer marks them as not needing frames).

## 9. Store Schema

```typescript
interface Viewport3DStoreState {
  gridLayout: ViewportGridLayout;
  panes: ViewportPaneConfig[];
  activePaneId: string;
  setGridLayout: (layout: ViewportGridLayout) => void;
  setPaneDisplayMode: (paneId: string, mode: DisplayMode) => void;
  setPaneCameraPreset: (paneId: string, preset: CameraPreset) => void;
  toggleCameraLink: (paneId: string) => void;
  setActivePane: (paneId: string) => void;
  maximisedPaneId: string | null;
  toggleMaximise: (paneId: string) => void;
}
```

## 10. Keyboard Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|---|---|
| `1` | Single viewport |
| `2` | Split horizontal |
| `3` | Split vertical |
| `4` | Quad viewport |
| `5` | One + two layout |
| `Space` | Maximise/restore active pane |
| `Ctrl+L` | Toggle camera linking for active pane |
| `Numpad 0` | Perspective preset |
| `Numpad 1` | Front |
| `Numpad 3` | Right |
| `Numpad 7` | Top |
| `Numpad 5` | Toggle perspective/orthographic |
